# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is public. The rules below keep a maintainer's working
# material out of it.
#
# WHY, and only why. A .gitignore is published like anything else, so a
# comment that inventories what a hidden file CONTAINS tells a reader exactly
# what was withheld -- it converts a silent absence into a described one.
# Say that a rule exists because the material is for whoever develops this
# project rather than for whoever uses it. Never say what is in it.
#
# Nothing here is secret. It is working material, and a consumer has no use
# for it. PUBLIC.md says that much, and deliberately no more.
#
# Each pattern below is anchored to the repository root with a leading "/".
# Unanchored, a pattern with no interior slash matches at ANY depth -- which
# would also swallow template/seed/'s own copies of these same names, the
# tracked payload a bootstrap installs from. Anchoring keeps the rule aimed
# at the installed, maintainer-only copies only.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/
/CLAUDE.md
/DEVELOPMENT-CHECKLIST.md
/BACKLOG.html
